# The generated shared seed catalogue is compared BYTE FOR BYTE by
# scripts/check-seed-drift.mjs: it re-runs the emitter and does a raw string
# comparison (`regeneratedText !== committed`) against the committed file.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, so without
# this entry a fresh clone writes the file with CRLF line endings while the Rust
# emitter always produces LF. The drift check would then fail on every clean
# checkout, reporting the file as STALE when nothing had drifted at all — and a
# guard that cries wolf gets disabled, which costs the guarantee it exists for.
#
# Pinned narrowly rather than repo-wide: a blanket `* text=auto` would
# renormalise every tracked file at once and bury this change in the diff.
seed/demo-outlet.json text eol=lf

# The identity files beside it, pinned for the same class of reason and one
# more (added 2026-09-17).
#
# The hash in seed/demo-outlet.json's `outlet_source_sha256` is now taken over
# NEWLINE-NORMALISED content, so the seeders no longer care how these are
# checked out -- that guard means "a different restaurant", not "a different
# line ending", and hashing raw bytes made five crash_durability tests fail on
# a Windows runner against an LF-authored catalogue.
#
# This entry is NOT what fixes that. It is here so the REPOSITORY STATES ITS
# LINE ENDINGS for the seed directory: without it, a file written by one tool
# and rewritten by another shows as modified with an EMPTY `git diff`, which
# costs somebody the minutes it takes to prove the content is identical. That
# happened on 2026-09-17 with edge/database/src/procurement/receipt.rs.
seed/*.toml text eol=lf
seed/*.json text eol=lf
